[06:08] I built and saved the phone agent for `pl-g7-multi-raw`. It has not been tested on any customers: `public-test-set.json` lists none for this brief, so I did not run `run_cases.py`. My checks were the static workflow check (0 errors, 0 warnings), local runs of the code steps and hooks, and a reading of the workflow against every rule in the brief and the two memos.
[06:08] 
[06:08] **How the call flows**
[06:08] - **Before the call:** a code step works out the calendar from `now` and the callback window. It applies memo OM-17 (21 October is a holiday, 26 October is a business day again).
[06:08] - **Opening and identity:** the agent confirms who is on the line, then asks the two security questions. A relative or other third party only gets asked when the customer can be reached.
[06:08] - **Loading the account:** once both security answers pass, `get_account` runs and the agent states every late product.
[06:08] - **Per product:** a code step computes the band, deadline, floor and the two persuasion offers. Car loan deadlines are capped at the 5th business day after today. For one test date I checked the deadlines by hand: 26 October for the late band, 22 October for the capped car loan.
[06:08] - **Ending the call:** each outcome has its own step that sends the fixed outcome and reason to `close_call`, then hangs up. No other bank tool can run after it.
[06:08] - **Outcome rules:**
[06:08]   - Any recorded promise forces outcome `promise`, unless the call is transferred.
[06:08]   - A transfer is closed as soon as `transfer_to_agent` succeeds, with no notes.
[06:08]   - A hook blocks any callback outside the allowed window, so an invalid one is never booked.
[06:08] 
[06:08] **Risks that only a test run would show**
[06:08] - **Notes for one-product customers:** the agent writes a note (`add_note`) for every product without a promise. That includes customers with only one product, because the multi-product rules say "this also applies when no product gets a promise". The close code list also says the single-product brief "never uses `add_note`", so the scorer may read this the other way.
[06:08] - **Choices left to the model:**
[06:08]   - which `no_promise` reason or `paid` outcome applies when no promise was recorded;
[06:08]   - writing all notes before ending the call;
[06:08]   - saying goodbye in the same message that ends the call.
[06:08] 
[06:08]   These rules are in the prompts but nothing in the graph enforces them.
[06:08] - **Blocked callbacks:** an out-of-window callback is sent to an address that does not exist, so nothing is booked. I could not check whether that failed request shows up in the bank's records.
[06:08] 
